<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Phocaea</h1><p class="st-meta">1275 CE – 1455 CE (approx.) · capital Phocaea</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Genoese lordship on the Aegean coast of Anatolia built on the alum mines that supplied Europe's textile industry.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1275 the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-viii-palaiologos">Michael VIII</a> granted <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/phocaea">Phocaea</a> and its alum mines to the Genoese brothers Manuel and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benedetto-zaccaria">Benedetto Zaccaria</a>. Alum, essential for fixing dyes in cloth, made the grant extremely valuable.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaccaria">Zaccaria</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-phocaea">New Phocaea</a> to protect the mines and dominated the European alum trade, shipping it to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-flanders">Flanders</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benedetto-zaccaria">Benedetto</a> also took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/chios">Chios</a> in 1304. The colony employed local Greek labour and paid tribute to Turkish neighbours. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> retook <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/phocaea">Phocaea</a> in 1340, but Genoese families, from the 1350s within the circle of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/maona-of-chios">Maona of Chios</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gattilusio">Gattilusio</a>, regained control and held it as Byzantine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-constantinople">conquest of Constantinople</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> took Old and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-phocaea">New Phocaea</a> in 1455, ending Genoese control of the alum trade until new mines were found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tolfa">Tolfa</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1275 CE – 1455 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.07%;width:3.58%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1275 CE – 1455 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Phocaea</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Manuel Zaccaria, Benedetto Zaccaria</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Latin Christianity, Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ligurian, Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Genoese Phocaea, Zaccaria Phocaea</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1365&amp;focus=lordship-of-phocaea" aria-label="Lordship of Phocaea on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5344 790 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Phocaea lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5664 1046L5709 970M5664 1046L5650 1056M5664 1046L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5650 1056h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5664 1046h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5664 1046h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Phocaea. <a href="/atlas?year=1365&amp;focus=lordship-of-phocaea">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

